# Step: feedback-ui

> Part of: [plan.md](../plan.md) · Spec: [spec.md](../spec.md)

## What This Step Delivers

Frontend feedback UI: a `FeedbackControls` component (thumbs up/down + comment input), a
`useFeedback` hook (lazy fetch, client cache, debounced PUT with AbortController), and
integration into `ClauseCard` and the overall score area. Hover-to-reveal with focus-lock
on comment input. After this step, users can submit and view feedback on completed reviews.

## Done When

- Hovering over a clause card or overall score area reveals thumbs up/down buttons + comment input
- Controls disappear on mouse leave unless comment input is focused
- First hover triggers a lazy bulk fetch of all feedback (review + clause)
- Thumbs clicks and text submissions fire debounced PUTs (300ms)
- Rapid toggles cancel in-flight requests (AbortController)
- Saved feedback is shown as selected on subsequent hovers
- Vote change clears comment (via PUT with no comment field)
- Feedback controls only appear on completed reviews

## Dependencies

- **feedback-api** must be complete (all 4 endpoints working)

## Cycles

### feedback-types

**Test** — write and confirm they fail:
- **test_feedback_schema_valid**: Validate `ReviewFeedbackSchema.parse({id: "...", review_id: "...", vote: "up", comment: null, created_at: "...", updated_at: "..."})` succeeds
- **test_feedback_schema_invalid_vote**: Validate with `vote: "maybe"` throws ZodError

Since these are Zod schemas in TypeScript, tests can be run via the project's frontend test
runner if one exists, or validated manually via `npx tsx` script. If no frontend test runner,
validate by type-checking: `npx tsc --noEmit`.

**Code** — Add to `frontend/app/evaluate-contract/types.ts`:
```typescript
export const VoteSchema = z.enum(["up", "down"]);

export const ReviewFeedbackSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  review_id: z.string().uuid(),
  vote: VoteSchema,
  comment: z.string().nullable(),
  created_at: z.string(),
  updated_at: z.string(),
});

export const ClauseFeedbackSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  clause_id: z.string().uuid(),
  vote: VoteSchema,
  comment: z.string().nullable(),
  created_at: z.string(),
  updated_at: z.string(),
});

export type Vote = z.infer<typeof VoteSchema>;
export type ReviewFeedback = z.infer<typeof ReviewFeedbackSchema>;
export type ClauseFeedback = z.infer<typeof ClauseFeedbackSchema>;
```

**Refactor** — none

**Commit**: `add feedback Zod schemas and types`

---

### use-feedback-hook

**Test** — Type-check via `npx tsc --noEmit`. No unit tests for hooks in this project
(no React testing library setup). The hook will be verified via browser in the Verification
section.

**Code** — Create `frontend/app/contract/[id]/useFeedback.ts`:

```typescript
import { useState, useRef, useCallback } from "react";
import type { Vote, ReviewFeedback, ClauseFeedback } from "@/app/evaluate-contract/types";
import { BACKEND_URL } from "@/app/evaluate-contract/constants";

interface FeedbackState {
  reviewFeedback: ReviewFeedback | null;
  clauseFeedback: Map<string, ClauseFeedback>; // keyed by clause_id
  loaded: boolean;
}

export function useFeedback(reviewId: string) {
  const [state, setState] = useState<FeedbackState>({
    reviewFeedback: null,
    clauseFeedback: new Map(),
    loaded: false,
  });
  const fetchedRef = useRef(false);
  const abortRef = useRef<AbortController | null>(null);
  const debounceRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null>(null);

  const fetchAll = useCallback(async () => {
    if (fetchedRef.current) return;
    fetchedRef.current = true;

    const [reviewRes, clauseRes] = await Promise.all([
      fetch(`${BACKEND_URL}/api/reviews/${reviewId}/feedback`),
      fetch(`${BACKEND_URL}/api/reviews/${reviewId}/clause-feedback`),
    ]);

    const reviewData = reviewRes.ok ? await reviewRes.json() : null;
    const clauseData: ClauseFeedback[] = clauseRes.ok ? await clauseRes.json() : [];

    setState({
      reviewFeedback: reviewData,
      clauseFeedback: new Map(clauseData.map((cf) => [cf.clause_id, cf])),
      loaded: true,
    });
  }, [reviewId]);

  const submitFeedback = useCallback(
    (
      target: { type: "review" } | { type: "clause"; clauseId: string },
      vote: Vote,
      comment?: string,
    ) => {
      // Clear any pending debounce
      if (debounceRef.current) clearTimeout(debounceRef.current);
      // Cancel in-flight request
      if (abortRef.current) abortRef.current.abort();

      // Optimistic update
      setState((prev) => {
        if (target.type === "review") {
          return {
            ...prev,
            reviewFeedback: {
              ...(prev.reviewFeedback || { id: "", review_id: reviewId, created_at: "", updated_at: "" }),
              vote,
              comment: comment ?? null,
            },
          };
        }
        const next = new Map(prev.clauseFeedback);
        next.set(target.clauseId, {
          ...(prev.clauseFeedback.get(target.clauseId) || {
            id: "", clause_id: target.clauseId, created_at: "", updated_at: "",
          }),
          vote,
          comment: comment ?? null,
        });
        return { ...prev, clauseFeedback: next };
      });

      // Debounced PUT
      debounceRef.current = setTimeout(async () => {
        const controller = new AbortController();
        abortRef.current = controller;

        const url =
          target.type === "review"
            ? `${BACKEND_URL}/api/reviews/${reviewId}/feedback`
            : `${BACKEND_URL}/api/reviews/clauses/${target.clauseId}/feedback`;

        const body: { vote: Vote; comment?: string } = { vote };
        if (comment !== undefined) body.comment = comment;

        try {
          const res = await fetch(url, {
            method: "PUT",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify(body),
            signal: controller.signal,
          });
          if (res.ok) {
            const data = await res.json();
            setState((prev) => {
              if (target.type === "review") {
                return { ...prev, reviewFeedback: data };
              }
              const next = new Map(prev.clauseFeedback);
              next.set(target.clauseId, data);
              return { ...prev, clauseFeedback: next };
            });
          }
        } catch (e) {
          if (e instanceof DOMException && e.name === "AbortError") return;
          // Silently fail — user can retry
        }
      }, 300);
    },
    [reviewId],
  );

  return { ...state, fetchAll, submitFeedback };
}
```

**Refactor** — none

**Commit**: `add useFeedback hook with lazy fetch and debounced upsert`

---

### feedback-controls-component

**Test** — Type-check via `npx tsc --noEmit`. Visual verification via browser.

**Code** — Create `frontend/app/contract/[id]/FeedbackControls.tsx`:

```tsx
"use client";

import { useState, useRef } from "react";
import type { Vote } from "@/app/evaluate-contract/types";

const THUMB_BASE = "p-1.5 rounded transition-colors text-sm";
const THUMB_SELECTED = "bg-foreground/10 text-foreground";
const THUMB_UNSELECTED = "text-foreground/30 hover:text-foreground/60";

interface FeedbackControlsProps {
  vote: Vote | null;
  comment: string | null;
  onSubmit: (vote: Vote, comment?: string) => void;
}

export default function FeedbackControls({ vote, comment, onSubmit }: FeedbackControlsProps) {
  const [localComment, setLocalComment] = useState(comment ?? "");
  const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);

  function handleVote(v: Vote) {
    if (v === vote) return; // No change
    setLocalComment(""); // Vote change clears comment
    onSubmit(v);
  }

  function handleCommentSubmit() {
    if (!vote) return; // Must have a vote first
    onSubmit(vote, localComment || undefined);
  }

  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2 mt-2" onMouseDown={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>
      <button
        type="button"
        onClick={() => handleVote("up")}
        className={`${THUMB_BASE} ${vote === "up" ? THUMB_SELECTED : THUMB_UNSELECTED}`}
        aria-label="Thumbs up"
        aria-pressed={vote === "up"}
      >
        👍
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        onClick={() => handleVote("down")}
        className={`${THUMB_BASE} ${vote === "down" ? THUMB_SELECTED : THUMB_UNSELECTED}`}
        aria-label="Thumbs down"
        aria-pressed={vote === "down"}
      >
        👎
      </button>
      {vote && (
        <input
          ref={inputRef}
          type="text"
          value={localComment}
          onChange={(e) => setLocalComment(e.target.value)}
          onBlur={handleCommentSubmit}
          onKeyDown={(e) => { if (e.key === "Enter") handleCommentSubmit(); }}
          placeholder="Add a comment..."
          className="flex-1 rounded border border-foreground/10 bg-transparent px-2 py-1 text-xs text-foreground/70 placeholder:text-foreground/30 focus:outline-none focus:border-foreground/30"
        />
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Refactor** — none

**Commit**: `add FeedbackControls component with thumbs and comment input`

---

### clause-card-integration

**Test** — Type-check via `npx tsc --noEmit`. Visual verification via browser.

**Code** — Modify `frontend/app/contract/[id]/ClauseCard.tsx`:

- Accept new props: `feedback: ClauseFeedback | null`, `onSubmit: (vote, comment?) => void`,
  `loaded: boolean`
- Add hover state + focus-lock logic
- Render `FeedbackControls` on hover when `loaded` is true

```tsx
"use client";

import { useState, useRef } from "react";
import type { FairnessRating, ReviewClause } from "@/app/evaluate-contract/types";
import type { ClauseFeedback, Vote } from "@/app/evaluate-contract/types";
import FeedbackControls from "@/app/contract/[id]/FeedbackControls";

// ... existing constants ...

export default function ClauseCard({
  clause,
  fairness,
  feedback,
  onFeedbackSubmit,
  feedbackLoaded,
  onHoverStart,
}: {
  clause: ReviewClause;
  fairness: FairnessRating;
  feedback: ClauseFeedback | null;
  onFeedbackSubmit: (vote: Vote, comment?: string) => void;
  feedbackLoaded: boolean;
  onHoverStart: () => void;
}) {
  const [hovered, setHovered] = useState(false);
  const [inputFocused, setInputFocused] = useState(false);
  const showFeedback = (hovered || inputFocused) && feedbackLoaded;

  return (
    <div
      className={`${CARD} border-l-2 ${FAIRNESS_BORDER[fairness]}`}
      onMouseEnter={() => { setHovered(true); onHoverStart(); }}
      onMouseLeave={() => setHovered(false)}
      onFocusCapture={() => setInputFocused(true)}
      onBlurCapture={(e) => {
        if (!e.currentTarget.contains(e.relatedTarget)) setInputFocused(false);
      }}
    >
      <h4 className={SECTION_HEADER}>
        <span className={SECTION_NUMBER}>{clause.section_number}</span>
        <span className={CLAUSE_TYPE}>{clause.clause_type}</span>
      </h4>
      <p className={EXPLANATION}>{clause.explanation}</p>
      {showFeedback && (
        <FeedbackControls
          vote={feedback?.vote ?? null}
          comment={feedback?.comment ?? null}
          onSubmit={onFeedbackSubmit}
        />
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Refactor** — none

**Commit**: `integrate feedback controls into ClauseCard with hover-to-reveal`

---

### page-integration

**Test** — Type-check via `npx tsc --noEmit`. Visual verification via browser.

**Code** — Modify `frontend/app/contract/[id]/page.tsx`:

- Import and use `useFeedback` hook in `EvaluationResults`
- Pass feedback state + callbacks down to `ClauseSection` → `ClauseCard`
- Add hover-to-reveal feedback on the `ScoreBadge` area

Update `EvaluationResults`:
```tsx
function EvaluationResults({ result }: { result: ReviewCompleted }) {
  const grouped = groupByFairness(result.clauses);
  const { reviewFeedback, clauseFeedback, loaded, fetchAll, submitFeedback } =
    useFeedback(result.id);
  const [scoreHovered, setScoreHovered] = useState(false);
  const [scoreInputFocused, setScoreInputFocused] = useState(false);
  const showScoreFeedback = (scoreHovered || scoreInputFocused) && loaded;

  return (
    <article className={PAGE_CONTAINER}>
      <h1 className={PAGE_TITLE}>Evaluation complete</h1>
      {result.overall_fairness && (
        <div
          className="mt-4"
          onMouseEnter={() => { setScoreHovered(true); fetchAll(); }}
          onMouseLeave={() => setScoreHovered(false)}
          onFocusCapture={() => setScoreInputFocused(true)}
          onBlurCapture={(e) => {
            if (!e.currentTarget.contains(e.relatedTarget)) setScoreInputFocused(false);
          }}
        >
          <ScoreBadge rating={result.overall_fairness} />
          {showScoreFeedback && (
            <FeedbackControls
              vote={reviewFeedback?.vote ?? null}
              comment={reviewFeedback?.comment ?? null}
              onSubmit={(vote, comment) =>
                submitFeedback({ type: "review" }, vote, comment)
              }
            />
          )}
        </div>
      )}
      {/* ... summary, call_to_action unchanged ... */}
      <div className="mt-6 space-y-3">
        {FAIRNESS_SECTION_ORDER.map((rating) => (
          <ClauseSection
            key={rating}
            rating={rating}
            clauses={grouped[rating]}
            clauseFeedback={clauseFeedback}
            feedbackLoaded={loaded}
            onHoverStart={fetchAll}
            onFeedbackSubmit={(clauseId, vote, comment) =>
              submitFeedback({ type: "clause", clauseId }, vote, comment)
            }
          />
        ))}
      </div>
      <Link href="/evaluate-contract" className={BACK_LINK}>
        Evaluate another contract
      </Link>
    </article>
  );
}
```

Update `ClauseSection` props to pass through feedback state and callbacks to `ClauseCard`.
Add `clauseFeedback`, `feedbackLoaded`, `onHoverStart`, `onFeedbackSubmit` props to
`ClauseSection` and thread them to each `ClauseCard`.

**Refactor** — none

**Commit**: `wire feedback into page and ClauseSection`

---

## Verification

```
1. Start backend: cd backend && uvicorn main:app --reload
2. Start frontend: cd frontend && npm run dev
3. Upload a contract and wait for evaluation to complete
4. Hover over the overall score badge — thumbs up/down should appear
5. Click thumbs down — button should highlight
6. Type a comment and press Enter or blur — comment saves
7. Hover away — controls disappear
8. Hover back — previous vote and comment are shown
9. Change vote to thumbs up — comment should clear
10. Hover over a clause card — feedback controls appear
11. Submit feedback on a clause — persists on re-hover
12. Reload the page — hover over same clause — previous feedback shown
13. Check network tab — first hover fires 2 GETs (review + clause feedback),
    subsequent hovers fire 0 GETs (cached)
14. Rapidly click up/down/up/down — network tab shows only one PUT (debounced)
15. While typing a comment, move cursor outside card boundary — controls stay
    visible because input is focused
16. Click outside to blur — controls disappear
```

Use Playwright screenshots if available. All 16 checks must pass.

